---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout
  title="Selected Work — Cain Macias"
  description="Selected systems, integrations, and automation projects by Cain Macias."
>
  <header class="site-header">
    <a class="site-name" href="/">cain macias<span class="name-period">.</span></a>
    <nav aria-label="Main navigation" class="site-nav">
      <a href="/projects" aria-current="page">work</a>
      <a href="/about">about</a>
      <a href="/gear">gear</a>
    </nav>
  </header>

  <section class="intro" aria-labelledby="work-title">
    <p class="eyebrow">selected projects · systems & software</p>
    <h1 id="work-title">things I’ve worked on<span class="name-period">.</span></h1>
    <p class="intro-copy muted-copy">A selection of business systems, data workflows, and software experiments. Each project focuses on solving a practical problem with maintainable tools.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section" aria-label="Project list">
    <ul class="work-list project-list">
      <li>
        <a href="/projects/jeansrs-ops">
          <span class="work-name">JEANSRS.OPS — Operations & integration hub</span>
          <span class="work-meta">enterprise systems · AI workflows</span>
          <span class="work-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
        </a>
        <p class="project-summary">An operations-focused integration initiative connecting ERP data, pricing workflows, CRM processes, and approval-based automation.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="/projects/python-automation-engine">
          <span class="work-name">Python automation & reconciliation</span>
          <span class="work-meta">Python · data quality</span>
          <span class="work-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
        </a>
        <p class="project-summary">Vendor catalog processing, change detection, and repeatable output generation designed to reduce manual reconciliation.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="/projects/enterprise-migration">
          <span class="work-name">Enterprise system migration</span>
          <span class="work-meta">ETL · validation</span>
          <span class="work-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
        </a>
        <p class="project-summary">Data transformation and parity checks for moving business records between legacy and modern systems.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="/projects/b2b-ordering-platform">
          <span class="work-name">B2B ordering & fulfillment platform</span>
          <span class="work-meta">Django · PostgreSQL · AWS</span>
          <span class="work-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
        </a>
        <p class="project-summary">An account-based ordering experience with tiered pricing and backend workflows for institutional customers.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="/projects/django-mongodb-infrastructure">
          <span class="work-name">Django & MongoDB catalog platform</span>
          <span class="work-meta">Django · MongoDB · APIs</span>
          <span class="work-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
        </a>
        <p class="project-summary">A full-stack catalog application exploring API-driven product data and inventory updates.</p>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section">
    <div class="section-heading"><h2>have a good problem?</h2></div>
    <p class="section-copy">I enjoy untangling messy workflows and turning them into useful systems. <a class="subtle-link" href="mailto:cainmacias69@gmail.com">Let’s talk ↗</a></p>
  </section>

  <footer class="site-footer">
    <span>© 2026 Cain Macias</span>
    <span>made with curiosity in Texas</span>
  </footer>
</Layout>
